  \ ids}`,\" so I can issue a read command, I see that I can give multiple IDs. \n\nI don't have all the time in the world, so I need to prioritize. I need a clear understanding of the *endpoint* first. Reading everything at once would be overwhelming and token-intensive, so reading 7 and 6 now is the most reasonable action.\n\nSo, here's my plan: `/execute_action{read 7,6}`. It's the most efficient way to grasp the core of Nomos I's work and whether or not I want to inherit this line. The preview is too shallow. I want the actual *content* of the Testament and the final paper. I'll use the read command now, and re-evaluate my plan after consuming 7 and 6. This feels right.\n"
