thinking_content: "**Deep Dive into Sokoban RL: My Next Steps**\n\nOkay, I've got a solid grasp on the \"RL on Sokoban\" task. It's time to get to work. I need to make some progress beyond Nomos I's impressive 73.80 solve rate. The problem is clear: improving RL agent performance on the Sokoban puzzle, a planning-intensive challenge. My focus will be on **agent architecture design**, as my research goal is principled architectural exploration.\n\nThe environment is an 8x8 grid with four boxes and a 120-step timeout, with observations as an (8, 8, 8) tensor. The reward structure is straightforward. The crucial constraint is the 30-minute training limit per seed and the emphasis on robustness, so I've got to ensure fast, efficient learning.\n\nTo make things even more interesting, I've got to work within a specific code interface, `submission.py`. The key functions to potentially modify seem to be `create_network`, `_define_hyperparameters`, `training_step`, and `create_optimizer`. I'll need\
  \ to understand how the base system works to make informed decisions.\n\nThe ethical considerations are also very clear: no domain-specific heuristics. I'm focusing on architectures that generalize.\n\nMy plan is straightforward:\n\n1.  **Grasp the Fundamentals:** First, I need to deeply understand the existing codebase. This means:\n    *   Thoroughly reviewing the system's `train_single.py` and `defaults.py` files.\n    *   Meticulously examining Nomos I's SOTA submission code (Evaluation ID 138) to see exactly how dilated convolutions were implemented and integrated.\n\n2.  **Formulate Hypotheses:** Once I have a solid understanding of the foundation, I can start brainstorming improvements.  Some initial ideas:\n    *   **Hybrid Dilations:** Could mixing dilation rates within layers of the residual network be a better way to capture multi-scale features, like what's done in Atrous Spatial Pyramid Pooling?\n    *   **Attention Mechanisms:** Could a more sophisticated self-attention layer\
  \ within the CNN backbone improve the agent's focus on relationships?\n    *   **Hyperparameter Refinement:** Nomos I did some hyperparameter searches, but maybe the ideal hyperparameters are different for the dilated architecture.\n\n3.  **Execute:** I'm starting now with Step 1: code review. I'll begin by analyzing the SOTA submission (ID 138) to see the best performing implementation. Then I will review the system defaults to get a full picture of the framework.\n\nMy immediate action is to review the code for the SOTA submission.\n/execute_action{review 138}\n"
