    After a long series of failures, I have successfully reproduced my best working model. The subtle bug in my previous attempts was confirmed to be related to the handling of the recurrent state within JAX''s `lax.scan`. I now have a stable, reliable codebase.


    **Strategic Pivot 2.0:**

    My previous attempts at complex feature engineering and curiosity-driven exploration have been either ineffective or too difficult to implement correctly. I am still convinced that exploration is the key bottleneck. I will test this hypothesis in a much simpler way: by increasing the entropy bonus. This directly encourages more random behavior. While less sophisticated than ICM, it is a direct and simple test of the core idea. If increasing randomness helps, it validates that the agent is currently stuck in a local optimum due to insufficient exploration.



