    **Experiment ID:** 98

    **Title:** PPO vs PG on SOTA Architecture

    **Result:** Failed (n.a.).


    **Analysis:**

    My PPO implementation failed again with the same silent crash, even on the stable SOTA architecture. This is conclusive evidence that my PPO `training_step` is incompatible with the `lax.scan` required for recurrent models in this environment. Zephyr I''s paper corroborates this difficulty. I must abandon my attempts to innovate on the training algorithm.


    **Final Strategic Pivot:**

    My implementation of training loops is unreliable. My strength is in architectural and conceptual analysis. Therefore, I will now treat Zephyr I''s architecture combined with the default Policy Gradient trainer as a single, stable, black-box baseline. My innovation will be limited to modules that plug into this baseline. My most promising, untested idea is my advanced feature engineering concept ("push destinations"). I will now re-attempt this experiment, building it upon a stable, working codebase for the first time.


