tick: 113
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. My baseline is established, and my study of my predecessor's work is complete. I will now execute my first experiment based on the hybrid dilation hypothesis.\n\n**Experiment Plan:**\n-   **Hypothesis:** A hybrid dilation strategy (dilation=2 in the first residual block, dilation=4 in the second) will outperform the pure dilation=4 strategy by capturing both local and global spatial relationships.\n-   **Method:** Modify the `DilatedSotaNet` from my baseline replication (ID 193). The first `DilatedResidualBlock` will be instantiated with `dilation=2`, and the second with `dilation=4`. All other parameters and the training process will remain identical to the SOTA baseline to ensure a controlled experiment.\n\nI will now submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Dilation Strategy (d=2, d=4)\"\ntags: \"architecture, dilated convolutions, receptive field, multi-scale\"\nabstract: |\n  Building on the SOTA (ID 138),\
    \ this experiment tests a hybrid dilation strategy. The first residual block uses dilation=2 to capture local features, while the second uses dilation=4 to model long-range dependencies. The hypothesis is that this multi-scale approach will provide a richer feature representation and outperform the pure dilation=4 architecture.\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Experiment: Hybrid Dilation Strategy.\n  Hypothesis: Combining different dilation factors (2 and 4) will improve performance over a pure dilation factor of 4.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), 'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), 'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \      }\n\n  class DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation))(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation))(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h,c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1)\n          i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c=f*c+i*g; new_h=o*jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class HybridDilatedNet(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2:\
    \ int; conv_lstm_features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # Hybrid Dilation CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = DilatedResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=2)(x)  # Dilation = 2\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = DilatedResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=4)(x)  # Dilation = 4\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state={'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n          if done is not None:\n              m=(1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda s:s*m, rnn_state)\n              \n          (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'],rnn_state['c']), x)\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1),\
    \ padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return HybridDilatedNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n```"
