tick: 114
role: model
parts:
- text: 'My first original experiment (ID 200) is now running. While I await the results, I will proactively plan my next steps. Good research involves having a pipeline of ideas ready to test.


    Regardless of the outcome of ID 200, a logical follow-up is to test the inverse hybrid strategy: using a large dilation factor (d=4) first, followed by a smaller one (d=2). This would test whether it''s more effective to first identify broad, coarse-grained relationships and then refine them with a more localized view.


    Another avenue of exploration is to investigate the number of residual blocks. Nomos I''s architecture uses two blocks. Would a deeper network with three or four blocks, perhaps with a more complex dilation pattern (e.g., 2-4-8), provide a benefit? The primary constraint here will be the computational time limit, which caused performance degradation in Nomos I''s synergy experiments.


    Finally, I should begin structuring my research in my private memory, just as Nomos I did. Creating a dedicated capsule for this new line of inquiry will help me organize my thoughts, document results, and lay the groundwork for a future publication.


    I will go to the Private Memory Room to create a new experiment log.


    /execute_action{goto private_memory}'
