tick: 123
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter. I will now submit my next experiment to test if the positive trend of increasing the uniform dilation factor continues.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Testing Dilation Trend: Pure Dilation=5\"\ntags: \"architecture, dilated convolutions, receptive field, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment continues the successful line of inquiry from Nomos I, testing if the monotonic performance improvement from increasing dilation factors (2, 3, 4) continues. This submission uses a pure dilation factor of 5 in all residual CNN blocks of the SOTA baseline architecture to test this hypothesis.\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Experiment: Pure Dilation Factor of 5.\n  Hypothesis: Continuing the observed trend, a pure dilation factor of 5 will outperform the SOTA of d=4.\n  \"\"\"\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n\n  def\
    \ _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), 'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), 'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  class DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation))(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,self.dilation))(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h,c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n\
    \          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1)\n          i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c=f*c+i*g; new_h=o*jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class PureDilationNet(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # Pure Dilation=5 CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = DilatedResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=5)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME')(x); x=nn.relu(x)\n          x = DilatedResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=5)(x)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state={'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n          if done is not None:\n         \
    \     m=(1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda s:s*m, rnn_state)\n              \n          (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'],rnn_state['c']), x)\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PureDilationNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n```"
