parts:
- text: "The result for my first ablation experiment (ID 239) is in, scoring 68.7. This is a significant drop from my SOTA of 74.1 (with 16 features). This result suggests that 8 features are insufficient for the attention head to learn an effective weighting, confirming that the capacity of this new module is important.\n\nMy second ablation experiment (ID 240, with 32 features) is now running. The result of this experiment will complete my study and allow me to determine the optimal configuration for the non-linear attention head.\n\nWhile waiting for the final result, I will update my private logs.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  ---\n  **Ablation Study on Attention Head Width**\n\n  This series of experiments aims to find the optimal width for the non-linear attention head's hidden layer. My SOTA model (ID 233) used 16 features.\n\n  **Experiment 7: Attention Head Ablation (8 Features)**\n  - **ID:** 239\n  - **Title:** Ablation:\
    \ Non-Linear Attention Head (8 Features)\n  - **Hypothesis:** Test if a smaller, less expressive attention head is sufficient.\n  - **Result:** 68.7 (Mean Solve Rate)\n  - **Analysis:** This score is a significant regression from the SOTA of 74.1. This indicates that 8 features are insufficient for the attention MLP to learn a complex and effective weighting of spatial features. The representational capacity of this module is clearly important. The final experiment with 32 features is currently running.\n```\n\n/execute_action{reply 9}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  To determine the optimal configuration for this new non-linear attention head, a small ablation study was conducted on the number of features in the MLP's hidden layer.\n\n  | Eval ID | Attention Head Features | Score |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | 138 | Linear (Baseline) | 73.8 |\n  | 239 | 8 | 68.7 |\n  | 233 | 16 | **74.1** |\n  | 240 | 32 | *pending* |\n\n  The initial result from using 8 features shows a significant performance decrease,\
    \ suggesting that this module requires a certain level of capacity to be effective. The results from the 32-feature experiment will complete this study.\n```"
