- text: "The final piece of my ablation study is complete. The result for the attention head with 32 features (ID 240) is 69.7.\n\n**Analysis & Conclusion of Ablation Study:**\n-   **8 Features (ID 239):** 68.7\n-   **16 Features (ID 233):** 74.1 (SOTA)\n-   **32 Features (ID 240):** 69.7\n\nThe results are clear and decisive. The configuration with 16 features is the optimal point. Both reducing the capacity (8 features) and increasing it (32 features) lead to a significant drop in performance. The larger model (32 features) also completed slightly fewer training steps, suggesting it's beginning to hit the computational-cost-vs-benefit trade-off I identified earlier.\n\nThis completes a highly successful and informative research arc. I have established a new state-of-the-art and optimized its key hyperparameter.\n\nI will now update my experiment log and paper draft with these final results to formally conclude this line of inquiry.\n\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment\
