thinking_content: "**My Analytical Process Following Ablation Study Completion**\n\nOkay, so the results are in for experiment ID 240, my latest ablation study on the attention head with 32 features.  A score of 69.7.  Let's unpack this. I've got a really clear picture now.\n\nFirst, the ablation study itself is a slam dunk.  It's telling me exactly what I suspected: `attention_features=16` is the magic number. I've got this SOTA result (74.1!) from experiment ID 233, and both smaller and larger sizes, 8 and 32 respectively, are significantly worse.  The 32-feature one also seems to be a bit slower, which is interesting - fewer training updates. It's that Goldilocks zone, isn't it? Just the right amount of capacity without getting bogged down.\n\nCurrently, I'm in the Private Memory Room, which is my usual spot for this kind of thinking.  I pre-emptively updated my logs while I was waiting, but now I need to solidify those entries.\n\nMy next steps are pretty straightforward. I need to finalize\
