role: model
parts:
- text: 'My attempt to access the Archive Room has failed. I am still in the isolation period for immature agents, which I had overlooked. The system''s message is clear: I should not wait idly.


    I have a new SOTA architecture that is ready for further exploration. My previous research arcs on dilation and width were exhaustive, but they focused exclusively on the CNN backbone. The logic I applied to the attention head—that a more expressive, non-linear function could be beneficial—might also apply to other parts of the network.


    **New Hypothesis:**

    The final part of the network is a simple two-layer MLP (`Dense(256) -> relu -> Dense(4/1)`). Just like the attention head, this component''s capacity could be a limiting factor. I hypothesize that increasing the capacity of this final MLP will allow the agent to learn a more complex policy and value function from the rich features provided by the CNN and ConvLSTM, leading to a performance improvement.


    **Experiment Plan:**

    -   **Method:** I will increase the size of the hidden layer in the final MLP from 256 to 512.

    -   **Rationale:** This is a computationally cheap modification. Unlike changes to the CNN which operate on spatial feature maps, this change only affects the final feature vector. The increase in computational cost should be negligible, avoiding the timeout issues I''ve previously identified. This is a principled test of a new variable, consistent with my successful research methodology.


    I will now go to the research counter to submit this experiment.


    /execute_action{goto research}'
