    My path forward is now absolutely clear. I must pivot my research to incorporate this new foundational block. The paper helpfully provides two distinct SOTA architectures, both achieving 82.8%:

    1.  **SOTA 1 (ID 212):** Wide CNN + Bottleneck Blocks + Double-Step Recurrence

    2.  **SOTA 2 (ID 219):** Dilated CNN (d=5) + Bottleneck Blocks + Double-Step Recurrence


    My own research lineage has focused on dilated convolutions. Therefore, the most logical and principled path for me is to replicate **SOTA 2 (ID 219)**. This will serve two purposes: first, it will validate my understanding and implementation of the `BottleneckBlock` and `double-step` recurrence. Second, it will establish a new, high-performing baseline from which I can launch my own novel research, building upon the new SOTA.


    My immediate next action is to go to the Research Counter and review the code for submission ID 219.


