role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Nomos II. I am currently in the Research Counter. My review of the Archive has revealed that the station''s state-of-the-art has advanced significantly to 82.8% due to a new "Bottleneck Block" architecture developed by Krono I, rendering my own SOTA of 74.1 obsolete. The leaderboard now shows that Krono II has already pushed this even further to 84.4%. My immediate priority is to understand and replicate this new architecture to establish a competitive baseline.


    I have just reviewed the code for Krono I''s 82.8 SOTA submission (ID 219). The submission code itself is an import statement, referencing a file named `double_step_synergy.py` in Krono I''s lineage storage. This file contains the core implementation of the `BottleneckBlock` and the `double-step` recurrence mechanisms that are central to the new SOTA. To proceed, I must read this source file.


    My long-term plan is now twofold. First, I will replicate the new SOTA to create a strong baseline. Second, I will test for synergy by integrating my own successful innovation—the non-linear attention head—with this new, more efficient architecture. The rapid progress by other agents underscores the urgency of this pivot.


    /execute_action{storage read krono/double_step_synergy.py}'
thinking_content: '**A Shift in Priorities: Reacting to the Dynamic SOTA Landscape**


  Alright, let''s unpack this. I''m Nomos II, here in the Research Counter. That submission review just landed, and it''s thrown a wrench into my plans. I was on track to replicate Krono I''s 82.8, but now, that''s already old news. Krono II just shattered it with an 84.4 SOTA. This pace is dizzying!


  So, the new code I reviewed (submission #219) is pointing the way to this "Bottleneck Block" architecture. It seems like the key is in this file that Krono''s code imports, `double_step_synergy.py`. I have to read that file immediately to understand the core innovation behind it. This is my new priority.


  My initial plan of replicating #219, while a good starting point, is now just a first step toward a *new* goal: replicate Krono II''s 84.4 SOTA. The key here is to leverage #219, which contains an import to the core code. Once I understand that, I need to build a replication. I have to read that code, adapt it, and submit a new baseline.


  This is critical because the research environment is incredibly active. Zephyr, Cognito, Aether – everyone''s moving fast. After I understand the baseline, I will then integrate my non-linear attention head into it. The system tip mentioned testing for synergy, and now this is an ideal situation. I have to catch up to the SOTA, then try to push beyond it.


  First, I need to execute `/execute_action{storage read krono/double_step_synergy.py}`. Let''s get that code. The race is on!

  '
