parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 154\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nomos II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the SOTA with principled architectural exploration.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 133,117 / 300,000 used (44%)\n- Agent Age: 56 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read krono/bottleneck_sota.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read krono/dilated_cnn_convlstm.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for krono/bottleneck_sota.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for krono/dilated_cnn_convlstm.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\
    \n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 270 | 1 | SOTA synthesis attempt: std-width Bottleneck(d=5) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM(64) + AttnPool (no FE) | Zephyr I | 154 | running |\n| 269 | 1 | Structured Attention (Fixed Hparams) - Debugging Trial File Error | Aether I | 154 | n.a. |\n| 268 | 1 | Ablation Study 2: Dilation Rate d=6 | Krono II | 153 | running |\n| 267 | 1 | Structured Attention for Relational Reasoning in Sokoban (Fixed Optimizer) | Aether I | 153 | n.a. |\n| 266 | 1 | Replicate wide 64/128 + ratio=0.31, ConvLSTM=44 (double-step+AttnPool) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 152 | 77.80 |\n| 265 | 1 | Replicate wide 64/128 + ratio=0.31, ConvLSTM=44 (double-step+AttnPool) — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 152 | 75.50 |\n| 264 | 1 | Ablation Study 1: Dilation Rate d=4 | Krono II | 151 | 80.60 |\n| 263 | 1 | Aether SOTA + Wider CNN Features (64, 128) - No FE | Cognito I | 151 | 80.00 |\n\
    | 262 | 1 | Structured Attention for Relational Reasoning in Sokoban (Fixed Dilated Conv) | Aether I | 151 | n.a. |\n| 261 | 1 | Structured Attention for Relational Reasoning in Sokoban | Aether I | 150 | n.a. |\n\nPage 1 of 27 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-27, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**krono/bottleneck_sota.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n# Re-using Zephyr's ConvLSTMCellLN as it is a proven component.\nfrom dilated_cnn_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n# My new architectural idea: a Bottleneck Residual Block\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # 1x1 conv to reduce channels, then 3x3 conv, then 1x1 to restore\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4,\
    \ (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n        # Add shortcut connection\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass BottleneckSOTANet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        # 1. Wide CNN Backbone with Bottleneck Blocks\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        # 2. Standard ConvLSTM\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),\
    \ jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n        new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n```\n---\n**krono/dilated_cnn_convlstm.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n# Foundational modules from Zephyr I's public work\nclass\
    \ ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    dilation: int = 1\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation)(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i=nn.sigmoid(i);f=nn.sigmoid(f);o=nn.sigmoid(o);g=jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c), h\n\n# My architecture with dilated convolutions\nclass DilatedCNNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n  \
    \  @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        # 1. Dilated CNN Backbone\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=2)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=2)(x)\n        \n        # 2. ConvLSTM (from Zephyr I)\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n        new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n        # 3. Attention Pooling (from\
    \ Zephyr I)\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
