tick: 157
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. My private log is updated, and I have successfully replicated the station's SOTA architecture, establishing a new personal baseline of 82.3.\n\nMy path forward is clear. I will now conduct a synergy experiment, combining the new efficient Bottleneck architecture with my own proven innovation: the non-linear attention head. This is my most promising avenue for making a novel contribution and potentially pushing the SOTA even further. I will use the optimal 16 features for the attention head, as determined by my previous ablation study.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: Bottleneck SOTA + Non-Linear Attention Head\"\ntags: \"synergy, bottleneck, attention, sota, architecture\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests for synergy between the new SOTA architecture (Bottleneck Blocks, double-step recurrence) and my previously successful innovation, the non-linear attention head. Having established a strong replication baseline\
    \ of 82.3 (ID 271), I will now integrate my optimized non-linear attention head (16 hidden features) into this architecture. The hypothesis is that the combination of a more efficient backbone and a more expressive attention mechanism will lead to a new state-of-the-art.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,\
    \ h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i=nn.sigmoid(i);f=nn.sigmoid(f);o=nn.sigmoid(o);g=jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class SynergyNet(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int; attention_features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # 1. Dilated CNN with Bottleneck Blocks\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation_rate, self.dilation_rate))(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation_rate,\
    \ self.dilation_rate))(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # 2. Double-Step ConvLSTM\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          rnn_state_1, _ = lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n          rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = rnn_state_2\n\n          # 3. My Non-Linear Attention Head\n          attn_hidden = nn.Conv(self.attention_features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out_2)\n          attn_hidden = nn.relu(attn_hidden)\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(attn_hidden)\n          \n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B,\
    \ -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out_2, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          # 4. Final MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'attention_features': tune.choice([16]), # My innovation\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SynergyNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n\
    \          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n          attention_features=hparams['attention_features']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10113\n```"
