role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 166\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nomos II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the SOTA with principled architectural exploration.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 166,684 / 300,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read krono/ppo_training_fixed.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for krono/ppo_training_fixed.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 294 | 1 | Replicate std-width nodil recommended (ratio=0.25, entropy=0.01) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 166 | running |\n| 293 | 1 | Replicate std-width nodil recommended (ratio=0.25, entropy=0.01) — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 166 | running |\n| 292 | 1 | PPO Ablation 1: Clip Epsilon 0.1 | Krono II | 164 | 84.00 |\n| 291 | 1 | Std-width nodil entropy sweep: entropy_coef ∈ {0.008,0.01,0.012} (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 163 | 86.40 |\n| 290 | 1 | NodIl bottleneck ratio=0.20 replicate — BASE_SEED=123 (std-width d=5, double-step LN-ConvLSTM) | Zephyr I | 162 | 84.90 |\n| 289 | 1 | NodIl bottleneck ratio=0.20 replicate — BASE_SEED=7 (std-width d=5, double-step LN-ConvLSTM) | Zephyr I | 162 | 84.30 |\n| 288 | 1 | PPO with SOTA Architecture (v2 - RNN Fix) | Krono II | 161 | 86.90 |\n| 287 | 1 | Replication: Krono II's SOTA (84.4) - Double-Step Synergy (No FE) | Cognito I | 161 | 81.70 |\n| 286 | 1 | Structured Attention (Default Training Step) | Aether I | 161 | n.a. |\n| 285 | 1 | NodIl bottleneck\
    \ ratio fine ablation (std-width d=5, double-step LN-ConvLSTM) | Zephyr I | 160 | 85.20 |\n\nPage 1 of 30 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-30, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**krono/ppo_training_fixed.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import jit, vmap, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n@jit\ndef calculate_gae(\n    rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n    values: jnp.ndarray,\n    dones: jnp.ndarray,\n    gamma: float = 0.97,\n    gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n    next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n    values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n    not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n    deltas = rewards\
    \ + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n    def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n        delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n        not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n        advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n        return advantage_t, advantage_t\n    _, advantages = lax.scan(\n        scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n    )\n    advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n    return advantages\n\ndef ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn(\n    network: Any,\n    optimizer: Any,\n    params: Any,\n    opt_state: Any,\n    batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n    observations = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n    rewards = batch['rewards']; dones = batch['dones']\n    old_values = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n    final_values = batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n    \n    advantages\
    \ = calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n    returns = advantages + old_values\n    \n    batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n    \n    def loss_fn(params):\n        if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n            def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n                env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n                def step_fn(carry, t):\n                    rnn_state = carry\n                    obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                    obs_b = obs[None, ...]; prev_done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n                    rnn_state_b = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state) if rnn_state is not None else None\n                    logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(params, obs_b, prev_done_b, rnn_state_b)\n                    logits = logits_b[0]; value = value_b[0]\n                    new_rnn_state\
    \ = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b) if new_rnn_state_b is not None else None\n                    return new_rnn_state, (logits, value)\n                _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n                return env_logits, env_values\n            all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n        else:\n            obs_reshaped = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n            dones_reshaped = dones.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length)\n            logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_reshaped, dones_reshaped)\n            all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length, -1)\n            all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n        \n        log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length),\
    \ actions\n        new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n        \n        ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n        advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n        clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n        \n        policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n        \n        returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n        \n        probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n        \n        total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n        return total_loss\n    \n    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n    updates, opt_state\
    \ = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    \n    return params, opt_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
