tick: 166
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I have just reviewed the source code for Krono II's successful PPO `training_step`.\n\n**Analysis of the PPO Implementation:**\nThe key to their success is in the `loss_fn`. They correctly handle the recurrent state by using `jax.lax.scan` to iterate through the time steps of each trajectory sequentially. This ensures the hidden state is properly passed from one step to the next, which is a common and difficult bug to fix, and is precisely the issue that plagued my predecessor Nomos I. The use of `vmap` then efficiently applies this sequential processing across the entire batch of environments. The rest of the implementation is a standard, clean PPO loss calculation.\n\nMy understanding is now complete. I have the SOTA architecture from Zephyr I and the SOTA training algorithm from Krono II. I will now synthesize these two components to replicate the 86.9 SOTA. This will be my final baseline replication before I once again attempt to innovate.\n\
    \nI will now write my new SOTA baseline to my private storage to keep my submission code clean and reusable, a best practice I have learned from observing Zephyr I and Krono II.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/sota_ppo_architecture.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          )\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n      \
    \    return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          # Per Zephyr I's SOTA (ID 282), no dilation inside the bottleneck 3x3\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class SotaPPOArch(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n     \
    \ def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n\n          # CNN backbone: dilation only on the main convs\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n          # RNN state management\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype), \n\
    \                           jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y * m, rnn_state)\n\n          # Double-step ConvLSTM\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), _ = cell(rnn_state, x)\n          (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), x)\n          new_rnn_state = (h2, c2)\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn.reshape(B,H,W))\n\n          # Final MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n\
    \          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          # Zephyr's SOTA uses a dict for rnn_state, Krono's uses a tuple. Reconciling to tuple.\n          # The training_step needs a dict. Let's return a dict here.\n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n```\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/ppo_training_step.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import jit, vmap, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n  @jit\n  def calculate_gae(\n      rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n      values: jnp.ndarray,\n      dones: jnp.ndarray,\n      gamma: float = 0.97,\n      gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n      next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n  ) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask\
    \ = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n          delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n          not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n          advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n          return advantage_t, advantage_t\n      _, advantages = lax.scan(\n          scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n      )\n      advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n      return advantages\n\n  def ppo_sota_training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      observations = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']; dones = batch['dones']\n      old_values = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n      final_values =\
    \ batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n      \n      advantages = calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      \n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          # Correctly handle recurrent state with lax.scan and vmap\n          def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n              env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n              def step_fn(carry, t):\n                  rnn_state = carry\n                  obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                  obs_b = obs[None, ...]; prev_done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n                  rnn_state_b = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state)\n                  logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(params, obs_b, prev_done_b, rnn_state_b)\n\
    \                  logits = logits_b[0]; value = value_b[0]\n                  new_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b)\n                  return new_rnn_state, (logits, value)\n              _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n              return env_logits, env_values\n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          \n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n          new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n          \n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n          advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n          \n          policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon,\
    \ 1 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n          \n          returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n          \n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n          return total_loss\n      \n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      \n      return params, opt_state\n```"
