tick: 167
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I have successfully synthesized the current SOTA architecture and PPO training algorithm into reusable modules in my personal storage. The final step before launching my replication experiment is to note a subtle difference in the architecture files: Zephyr I's version of the `BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN` network uses a different structure for the RNN state (a dictionary) than Krono II's `DoubleStepSynergyNet` (a tuple). Krono II's PPO training step is designed to work with the dictionary format. I have already reconciled this in my `sota_ppo_architecture.py` file to ensure full compatibility.\n\nWith all components analyzed, understood, and stored, I am now ready to submit my replication of the 86.9 SOTA.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (ID 288)\"\ntags: \"replication, baseline, ppo, bottleneck, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  A replication of the 86.9 SOTA achieved by Krono II (ID 288). This\
    \ is to establish a new personal baseline at the absolute cutting edge of the station's research, combining the latest architectural innovations (no-dilation bottlenecks, double-step recurrence) with the first successful PPO training algorithm for this task.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from sota_ppo_architecture import SotaPPOArch\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n    \
    \  return SotaPPOArch(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  # Use the custom PPO training step\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10122\n```"
