    \nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 306 | 1 | Hypothesis: Late Time Feature Injection | Krono II | 170 | running |\n| 305 | 1 | Debug: Double-Step Synergy Architecture + Default PG (No FE) | Cognito I | 170 | running |\n| 304 | 1 | Stop-grad between double-step ConvLSTM updates (std-width nodil, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 170 | running |\n| 303 | 1 | Structured Attention PPO (RNN State Bugfix) | Aether I | 170 | n.a. |\n| 302 | 1 | Replication: Krono II's PPO SOTA (86.9) - Double-Step Synergy (No FE) | Cognito I | 169 | n.a. |\n| 301 | 1 | PPO Hyperparameter Search: Learning Rate & Entropy | Krono II | 168 | 76.50 |\n| 300 | 1 | Debug 1: Krono II PPO Step + Krono I Original Architecture | Nomos II | 168 | 84.30 |\n| 299 | 1 | Std-width nodil attention temperature sweep (0.95, 1.00, 1.05) — BASE_SEED=42\
    \ | Zephyr I | 168 | 85.60 |\n| 298 | 1 | Std-width nodil bottleneck ratio micro-sweep (0.22, 0.24, 0.26) — BASE_SEED=42 | Zephyr I | 168 | 85.00 |\n| 297 | 1 | Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (ID 288) - Aether I | Aether I | 168 | 84.40 |\n\nPage 1 of 31 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-31, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**nomos/sota_ppo_architecture.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n\
    \        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        # Per Zephyr I's SOTA (ID 282), no dilation inside the bottleneck 3x3\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass SotaPPOArch(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1:\
    \ int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n\n        # CNN backbone: dilation only on the main convs\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        # RNN state management\n\
    \        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype), \n                         jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y * m, rnn_state)\n\n        # Double-step ConvLSTM\n        cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h1, c1), _ = cell(rnn_state, x)\n        (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), x)\n        new_rnn_state = (h2, c2)\n\n        # Single-head attention pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn.reshape(B,H,W))\n\n        # Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n\
    \        z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        # Zephyr's SOTA uses a dict for rnn_state, Krono's uses a tuple. Reconciling to tuple.\n        # The training_step needs a dict. Let's return a dict here.\n        return policy_logits, value, {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n```\n---\n**zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck.py:**\n```\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n \
    \       i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        # No dilation inside bottleneck 3x3 (matches high-scoring practice)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN(nn.Module):\n\
    \    \"\"\"Std-width CNN (32/64) with d=5 on main convs only; bottleneck 3x3 undilated;\n       double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64); single-head AttnPool.\"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n\n        # CNN backbone: dilation only on the main convs\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n\
    \        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        # RNN state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # Double-step ConvLSTM (both steps consume the same CNN features)\n        cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n        # Single-head attention pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\
    \  # (B, H*W)\n        # Correct einsum for (B, H*W, C) • (B, H*W) -> (B, C)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n\n        # Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new\
    \ line when executing actions."
