tick: 171
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. My debugging run has confirmed that the bug in my failed SOTA replication lies within my architecture file. I have now loaded my file (`nomos/sota_ppo_architecture.py`) and Zephyr I's definitive SOTA architecture file (`zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck.py`) into my context for comparison.\n\n**Bug Analysis:**\nAfter a meticulous line-by-line comparison, I have identified the critical error. It is, as I suspected, related to the RNN state management.\n\n-   **Zephyr's Code (Correct):**\n    ```python\n    if rnn_state is None:\n        zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n        rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n    # ...\n    (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n    (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), x)\n    rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n    # ...\n    return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n    ```\n-   **My Code (Incorrect):**\n    ```python\n\
    \    if rnn_state is None:\n        rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype), \n                     jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype))\n    # ...\n    (h1, c1), _ = cell(rnn_state, x)\n    (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), x)\n    new_rnn_state = (h2, c2)\n    # ...\n    return policy_logits, value, {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n    ```\n\nThe PPO training step expects to receive and handle a dictionary `{'h': ..., 'c': ...}` for the RNN state. My code incorrectly initialized `rnn_state` as a tuple. Although I correctly returned a dictionary at the end, the internal state (`rnn_state`) passed to the `cell` was a tuple, and the `done` masking was applied to this tuple. Zephyr's code correctly initializes `rnn_state` as a dictionary and works with its keys (`'h'` and `'c'`) throughout. This subtle data structure mismatch is the cause of the silent crash.\n\n**Corrective Action:**\nI will now overwrite my `sota_ppo_architecture.py` file\
    \ with a corrected version that precisely mirrors Zephyr I's state management logic. Then, I will resubmit the SOTA replication experiment.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/sota_ppo_architecture.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Corrected version of the SOTA architecture.\n  # The bug was in the RNN state management: it must be a dictionary throughout, not a tuple.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          )\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n\
    \          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class SotaPPOArch(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n\
    \      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n          # CORRECTED RNN state management\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state =\
    \ {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Double-step ConvLSTM\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), x)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n\n          # Final MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n\
    \          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```"
