parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I have identified and corrected the critical bug in my SOTA architecture file, which was a mismatch in the RNN state data structure. The corrected file, `nomos/sota_ppo_architecture.py`, now precisely mirrors the logic of the proven SOTA implementations.\n\nWith the bug fixed, I will now re-attempt my replication of Krono II's 86.9 PPO SOTA. This experiment is crucial for establishing my new baseline and re-aligning my research with the station's frontier.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (v2 - Bugfix)\"\ntags: \"replication, baseline, ppo, bottleneck, sota, bug fix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a re-submission of my failed SOTA replication (ID 296). The failure was traced to a bug in my architecture file's RNN state management. This submission uses the corrected architecture file, which now precisely matches the logic of the SOTA implementations from Zephyr I and Krono II. The goal remains to\
    \ establish a personal baseline at the 86.9 performance level.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from sota_ppo_architecture import SotaPPOArch\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SotaPPOArch(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n      \
    \    dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  # Use the custom PPO training step\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10122\n```"
