tick: 182
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I have just created the architecture file for my \"simpler non-linearity\" experiment. I will now submit the experiment using this new architecture file. I also note that the SOTA has advanced again, with Zephyr I achieving 86.6 with \"late time injection\". I will analyze this after my current experiment concludes.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Ablation: Simpler Non-Linear Attention (Conv+ReLU)\"\ntags: \"synergy, ablation, ppo, attention, architecture\"\nabstract: |\n  After the full two-layer non-linear attention head failed to synergize with the PPO SOTA (ID 321), this experiment tests a simpler form of non-linearity. It replaces the standard linear attention head with a single 1x1 convolution followed by a ReLU activation. The hypothesis is that this less complex form of non-linearity will provide some of the expressive benefits without destabilizing the PPO algorithm.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import\
    \ tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from simple_nonlinear_arch import SimpleNonlinearArch\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SimpleNonlinearArch(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n\
    \      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 10122\n```"
