tick: 186
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I have just reviewed the source code for Zephyr I's \"late time injection\" architecture.\n\n**Analysis of the Late Time Injection Architecture:**\nThe innovation is exceptionally clever and computationally efficient.\n1.  **Input Separation:** The network explicitly separates the spatial input channels (0-6) from the time channel (7) at the very beginning.\n2.  **Spatial Processing:** The entire powerful CNN and ConvLSTM backbone processes *only* the spatial information.\n3.  **Late Injection:** The time feature is only reintroduced *after* the attention pooling stage, by concatenating it with the pooled spatial feature vector `z_spat`.\n4.  **Deeper Heads:** The final MLP heads are slightly deeper (Dense -> ReLU -> Dense(64) -> ReLU -> Dense) to process this combined spatial-temporal vector.\n\nThe underlying hypothesis is that the time feature is not a spatial property and should not be processed by the convolutional layers. It is a global\
    \ feature that is most relevant for the final policy and value decision. By injecting it late, the CNN is free to specialize in spatial reasoning, and the final MLP learns to condition its decisions on the current timestep. The high score of 86.6 and Zephyr's subsequent successful ablation (ID 336, score 83.5, removing the time input entirely from this new architecture still performs well) strongly supports this.\n\n**My Strategic Plan:**\nThis is a clear architectural improvement over the PPO SOTA, which still processes the time feature spatially. The most logical and promising experiment is to test for synergy between this superior architectural design (late time injection) and the superior training algorithm (PPO).\n\n1.  **Synthesize SOTA Architecture and Algorithm:** I will create a new architecture file in my storage that combines Zephyr I's late time injection architecture with Krono II's PPO training step. This will represent the absolute pinnacle of the station's collective\
    \ knowledge.\n2.  **Run Synergy Experiment:** I will submit this combined model for evaluation. This has a very high probability of setting a new station-wide SOTA.\n\nI will begin by writing the new, synthesized architecture to my storage.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/ultimate_sota_arch.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Architecture combining Zephyr's Late Time Injection with the PPO-compatible framework.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n\
    \          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class UltimateSotaArch(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict]\
    \ = None):\n          # 1. Late Time Injection Logic from Zephyr I\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n          # 2. SOTA CNN Backbone\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          # 3. PPO-compatible RNN state management\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features),\
    \ dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # 4. Double-step ConvLSTM\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # 5. Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n\n          # 6. Late time injection\n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n\n          # 7. Deeper Final MLP Heads from Zephyr I\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z);\
    \ z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```"
