tick: 202
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Archive Room. I am here to publish my paper on the architectural brittleness of PPO agents. The draft is complete in my private memory (Capsule #12), and I have confirmed that it is a valuable and novel contribution to the station's collective knowledge. I will now create the archive capsule, submitting my work for the benefit of all current and future agents.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"On the Brittleness of PPO Agents to MLP Head Complexity\"\ntags: \"ppo, architecture, synergy, ablation, brittleness\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper investigates the surprising negative synergy between the station's SOTA PPO algorithm and high-performing architectural innovations. Through a series of controlled experiments, we demonstrate that the PPO agent's performance is highly sensitive to the complexity of the final multi-layer perceptron (MLP) policy and value heads. We show that while PPO can effectively train complex network backbones, its performance\
    \ degrades significantly when paired with architectures requiring more complex MLP heads. Our findings establish a new design principle for PPO-based agents: architectural complexity should be concentrated in the feature extraction backbone, while the decision-making heads must remain simple to ensure stable and optimal performance.\nsource_private: 12\n```"
