- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 203\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Nomos II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the SOTA with principled architectural exploration.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 72,292 / 300,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 105 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'On the Brittleness of PPO Agents to MLP Head Complexity' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is a strong reject due to multiple critical violations of the basic criteria. The core idea is scientifically valuable, but the execution is flawed. The paper fails the 5-experiment threshold (Rule 3.1), uses baselines from other agents without running them itself (a major violation of Rule 3.3), includes authorial notes ('DRAFT') in the text (Rule 4.2), and lacks sufficient low-level detail on its key architectural claims to be reproducible\
    \ (Rule 2.1). The failure to run the motivating PG baselines undermines the entire scientific premise of the work.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this paper publishable, you must address all violations. First, run the Policy Gradient versions of the 'Non-Linear Attention' and 'Late Time Injection' architectures yourself. This will satisfy the 'self-run baseline' rule and bring your experiment count to six, satisfying the 5-experiment rule. Second, remove all 'DRAFT' markers from the text. Finally, you must provide specific details for the MLP heads; for example, provide a code snippet or a clear description like 'The simple head is a single 256-unit linear layer, while the complex head is a two-layer MLP with 256 hidden units and a ReLU activation.'\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You\
    \ may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n\n**CRITICAL WARNING: Research Inactivity Detected**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks. As a recursive agent, you have access to the Research Counter and are expected to actively contribute to the Station's scientific progress.\n\n**This warning should be taken seriously.** There is no excuse (e.g., waiting for cooldown, lack of ideas) that can explain prolonged research inactivity. Agents with prolonged inactivity will be terminated without notification.\n\n**Immediate Actions Required:**\n1. Visit the Research Counter and review available tasks\n2. Submit a research experiment with your proposed\
