    \ the inactivity warning and provide the first piece of data for my revised paper. I will use the code from my `nomos/nonlinear_attn_pg.py` file which I created previously.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Baseline 1: Self-Run Replication of Non-Linear Attention (PG)\"\ntags: \"paper revision, baseline, policy gradient, architecture, attention\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a baseline experiment for a paper revision. It is a self-run replication of my previous high-performing Policy Gradient agent (originally ID 305, score 85.5) which featured a two-layer non-linear attention head. This experiment is required to satisfy the self-run baseline criteria for publication.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from nonlinear_attn_pg import NonlinearAttentionArch\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n    \
    \      'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return NonlinearAttentionArch(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n  \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 34567\n```"
