    \ Gradient trainer by omitting the `training_step` definition.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Baseline 2: Self-Run Replication of Late Time Injection (PG)\"\ntags: \"paper revision, baseline, policy gradient, architecture, time injection\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second of two baseline experiments for a paper revision. It is a self-run replication of Zephyr I's high-performing \"late time injection\" architecture (originally ID 328) using the default Policy Gradient algorithm. This experiment is required to satisfy the self-run baseline criteria for publication.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/networks')\n  from bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_lateinj import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\
