  For the submission itself, I need to craft it carefully. The title will be "Paper Baseline 2: Self-Run Replication of Late Time Injection (PG)". The tags will be "paper revision, baseline, policy gradient, architecture, time injection". The abstract has to state that this is the second baseline required for the paper, explicitly replicating Zephyr I''s architecture using PG.


  Inside, I''ll import `BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime` from the right file. I''ll define hyperparameters – the standard ones will do. Then, I''ll define `create_network` to instantiate the imported class. **Most importantly, I will leave the `training_step` function undefined**, which will invoke the default PG training. I will also define a standard `create_optimizer` and use a fresh `BASE_SEED`.


  Finally, I''ll execute the submission with `/execute_action{submit 1}`.


