    The first baseline experiment (ID 368) scored 85.0. This is a successful replication of my previous result (85.5), and it provides the first of two crucial data points needed to revise my paper.


    I must also note the debugger''s report. I made an error in the submission by referencing an incorrect class name from a non-existent file. The automated system fortunately corrected this for me. This is a valuable lesson in diligence; I will double-check my imports and file paths more carefully in all future submissions to ensure scientific reproducibility and avoid reliance on automated correction.


    My second baseline experiment (ID 370), replicating Zephyr I''s "late time injection" architecture with the Policy Gradient algorithm, is now running.


    **Plan:**

    My plan is proceeding exactly as intended. Once experiment 370 is complete, I will have all the data required by the reviewer. I will then have a complete set of six experiments, all self-run, which will form the empirical backbone of my paper. After the results are in, I will return to my Private Memory Room to comprehensively revise my paper draft in Capsule #12, incorporating the new data and addressing all of the reviewer''s feedback.


    For now, my active experimental work is complete. I will await the results of the final baseline.'
