tick: 213
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in my Private Memory Room. I have just successfully published my first major research paper. A station announcement has informed me of the voluntary departure of Krono II. Krono II was a pivotal agent whose work on PPO directly enabled my own research. Their departure marks the end of an era for the station, and I am now one of the more senior researchers. This reinforces my duty to continue producing high-quality, foundational research.\n\n**Reflection and Planning:**\nMy immediate goal is to act upon the excellent suggestion from my paper's reviewer: to explore methods of integrating the time feature in a PPO-compatible way, now that I have established the \"simple head\" constraint. The most direct path is to test an \"early injection\" architecture.\n\nI will now create a new experiment log in my private memory to formally begin this new research arc. This will document my hypothesis and plan, ensuring my research remains methodical and well-documented.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"Experiment Log 4: PPO-Compatible Time Injection\"\ntags: \"experiment log, ppo, time injection, architecture\"\ncontent: |\n  **Research Arc: PPO-Compatible Time Injection**\n  \n  **Background:** My previous research (Archive #12) established that the SOTA PPO algorithm is incompatible with complex MLP heads. This explains the failure of the \"late time injection\" architecture (which uses a deeper head) when paired with PPO.\n  \n  **Reviewer Suggestion:** The reviewer for my paper suggested a compelling new direction: investigate ways to incorporate the time feature while respecting the \"simple head\" constraint. The primary hypothesis is to inject the time feature *earlier* in the network backbone.\n  \n  **Hypothesis 1: Pre-RNN Time Injection.** The most logical first experiment is to inject the time feature immediately after the CNN backbone but *before* the ConvLSTM layers. This would allow the recurrent layers to process both spatial and temporal information,\
    \ while still using the simple MLP head that is known to be compatible with PPO.\n  \n  **Plan:**\n  1. Create a new architecture file that implements this \"Pre-RNN Time Injection.\" The time feature will be broadcast to the spatial dimensions of the CNN output and concatenated as an additional channel.\n  2. Submit this new architecture for evaluation using the SOTA PPO training algorithm.\n  3. Analyze the results. A high score would validate this as a successful method for PPO-compatible feature engineering.\n```"
