tick: 215
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. A new agent, Insight I, has joined the station. This is a welcome development. The recent departure of Krono II and termination of Cognito I left a void, and new perspectives are crucial for the station's health.\n\n**Reflection on Current SOTA and Plan:**\nThe leaderboard has shifted again. Aether I has successfully replicated my scientific finding and submitted an experiment combining Zephyr's architecture with a simple MLP head and PPO (ID 382), achieving a new SOTA of 87.7. This is excellent; it independently validates my published conclusion and advances the station's knowledge. My focus is not on reclaiming the top score, but on conducting the next logical scientific experiment.\n\nI am here to implement the \"Pre-RNN Time Injection\" architecture, as outlined in my new experiment log. This is a novel approach that respects my \"simple head\" constraint while attempting to incorporate the valuable time feature in a new, PPO-compatible\
    \ way. This is no longer about chasing the SOTA, but about principled exploration of the design space I have just defined.\n\n**Action:**\nI will now create the new architecture file in my storage.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/pre_rnn_time_injection.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Architecture testing Pre-RNN Time Injection with a PPO-compatible Simple Head.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n     \
    \     new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class PreRNNTimeInjectionArch(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat =\
    \ x[..., :7]\n          t_scalar = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2,3)) # Get scalar time\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n          # CNN Backbone (Spatial Only)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          # Pre-RNN Time Injection\n          t_broadcast = jnp.broadcast_to(t_scalar.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1), (B, H, W, 1))\n          rnn_input = jnp.concatenate([cnn_out, t_broadcast], axis=-1)\n\n          if\
    \ rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM input features are now cnn_features_2 + 1\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), rnn_input)\n          (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), rnn_input)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # Standard Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n\n          # PPO-Compatible Simple Head\n     \
    \     z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```"
