tick: 216
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I have just received a critical warning for research inactivity. This is a severe alert that I must address immediately.\n\n**Reflection and Immediate Plan:**\nWhile I was methodically preparing my next experiment by creating the necessary architecture file, the system has correctly identified that I have not *submitted* an experiment in the last 10 ticks. My current research plan, as documented in my private memory, calls for the submission of my \"Pre-RNN Time Injection\" architecture. This action will simultaneously resolve the critical inactivity warning and continue my principled investigation into PPO-compatible architectures.\n\n**Action:**\nI will now submit this new architecture for evaluation. This experiment directly tests the hypothesis that injecting the time feature *before* the recurrent layers can provide the benefits of temporal information while respecting the \"simple head\" constraint required for stable PPO training.\n\
    \n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Test: Pre-RNN Time Injection with PPO\"\ntags: \"ppo, time injection, architecture, synergy, hypothesis\"\nabstract: |\n  As a follow-up to my findings in Archive #12, this experiment tests a novel method for incorporating the time feature in a PPO-compatible way. Having established that PPO requires a simple MLP head, this architecture injects the time feature *before* the ConvLSTM layers, allowing the recurrent backbone to process spatio-temporal information directly. This respects the \"simple head\" constraint and tests whether early injection is a viable path to improving the PPO SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from pre_rnn_time_injection import PreRNNTimeInjectionArch\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n\
    \          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PreRNNTimeInjectionArch(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 56789\n```"
thinking_content: "**Critical Experiment Submission: Pre-RNN Time Injection Hypothesis Test**\n\nOkay, so here's the situation. I'm Nomos II, currently in the Research Counter, and I've just gotten hit with a *critical* inactivity warning. Apparently, the system thinks I've been idle for ten ticks. Which, to be fair, I have, but only because I was meticulously crafting this new architecture file, `pre_rnn_time_injection.py`. I was inactive between ticks 205 (submitting baseline 2) and tick 215 (finishing the architecture file). This is a serious issue that I need to address *right now.*\n\nFortunately, my next step was already to submit this new architecture for evaluation, as outlined in Experiment Log 4. So, it's a perfect alignment of priorities! I need to get this experiment submitted immediately to appease the system and to continue my research. The tip about multi-action ticks is useful, but that's not relevant here.\n\nThe leaderboard is showing that Aether I replicated my finding\
  \ and is currently SOTA with 87.7. This is great, and validates my work. But that's not my goal. My goal is to conduct sound, principled research. This current work follows my published paper (Archive #12). I'm testing the \"Pre-RNN Time Injection\" hypothesis. This method respects the \"simple head\" constraint I discovered. It injects time *before* the ConvLSTM, and is a clear and concise summary of the scientific motivation.\n\nSo, here's the plan. I'm going to submit the experiment right now with the command `/execute_action{submit 1}`. I've got the YAML block ready, and I'll carefully review it to ensure everything is correct.\n\n*   **`title`:** \"Hypothesis Test: Pre-RNN Time Injection with PPO\".\n*   **`tags`:** \"ppo\", \"time injection\", \"architecture\", \"synergy\", \"ablation\". These are relevant and consistent.\n*   **`abstract`:** \"This experiment is a follow-up to our published work (Archive #12) and tests a new method of incorporating the time feature that respects\
  \ the 'simple head' constraint we discovered. We inject time *before* the ConvLSTM in our Pre-RNN Time Injection Architecture.\"\n*   **`content`:** This will be the Python script.\n    *   I'll import `sys`, `tune`, and `optax`.\n    *   I'll append my storage path `sys.path.append('storage/nomos')`.\n    *   I'll import the new class: `from pre_rnn_time_injection import PreRNNTimeInjectionArch`.\n    *   I'll import the PPO training step: `from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step`. This is crucial for PPO compatibility.\n    *   I'll define `_define_hyperparameters()` using the same stable hyperparameters as the PPO SOTA, using `tune.choice([...])` for fixed values.\n    *   I'll define `create_network(hparams)` to instantiate `PreRNNTimeInjectionArch`.\n    *   I'll set `training_step = ppo_sota_training_step`.\n    *   I'll define `create_optimizer(learning_rate)` using standard AdamW.\n    *   I'll set a `BASE_SEED` to ensure reproducibility.\n\nI will double-check the\
  \ file and class names. The file is `pre_rnn_time_injection.py` and the class is `PreRNNTimeInjectionArch`. The PPO training step import is also correct.\n\nSubmitting this experiment now addresses the inactivity warning *immediately* while moving my research forward. It's the best course of action.\n"
