- text: "I am Nomos II, in my Private Memory Room. My experiment testing \"Pre-RNN Time Injection\" failed, which has led me to conclude my research arc on time-based features. The station has just announced the arrival of a new agent, Kairos I, and a highly relevant new paper from Aether I which formalizes the SOTA that was built upon my own published findings.\n\n**Reflection and Plan Adjustment:**\nThe arrival of a new agent is a positive sign for the station's cognitive diversity. More importantly, Aether I has now published the definitive paper on the SOTA architecture (Archive #13). As this SOTA is a direct successor to my own research line, it is a matter of scientific due diligence for me to read their paper. It will serve as the final piece of knowledge I need before pivoting my research to a new paradigm, ensuring I have a complete understanding of the paradigm I am leaving behind.\n\nMy plan is therefore adjusted:\n1.  **Log Final Result:** First, I will log the failure of my\
    \ last experiment in my \"Time Injection\" experiment log (Capsule #13) to formally close that chapter of my research.\n2.  **Read SOTA Paper:** Second, I will immediately proceed to the Archive Room to read Aether I's new paper. This will be my final act of engagement with the current SOTA before I begin exploring GNNs.\n\n/execute_action{reply 13}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Conclusion of Research Arc**\n  \n  **Experiment 1 (ID 388): Pre-RNN Time Injection.**\n  - **Score:** 81.5\n  - **Outcome:** Hypothesis Falsified.\n  \n  **Analysis:** Injecting the time feature into the recurrent backbone before the ConvLSTM layers is highly detrimental to performance, resulting in a score significantly lower than the no-time-injection baseline. This concludes my investigation into time injection methods. The collective evidence from my work (Archive #12) and Aether I's SOTA (Archive #13) strongly indicates that the optimal approach is to keep the time feature entirely separate from the spatial\
    \ backbone and only introduce it late in the network, using a PPO-compatible simple MLP head.\n```\n/execute_action{goto archive}"
