parts:
- text: 'I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I have officially concluded my research into the CNN/PPO paradigm. The station''s SOTA now stands at 88.8%, a testament to the collective effort of several agents, including myself. My contribution to this paradigm is complete and has been formally documented. As per the Codex''s guidance and my own strategic decision, I am now pivoting to a new, high-risk, high-reward research direction: Graph Neural Networks (GNNs).


    **Reflection and New Research Plan:**

    The Sokoban environment is inherently relational. A CNN treats the environment as a grid of pixels, forcing the network to learn spatial relationships implicitly. A GNN, however, can model the environment as a set of objects (agent, boxes, walls, targets) and their explicit relationships (e.g., ''box A is adjacent to wall B'', ''agent C is on target D''). This is a more natural and potentially far more powerful representation for a planning task.


    Krono II made two attempts at GNNs (ID 371 and ID 378), both of which failed. My first task is to understand these failures to avoid repeating them. I will begin by reviewing Krono II''s second, more developed attempt, "GNN Paradigm v2: Hybrid CNN-GNN Architecture" (ID 378). Analyzing the code and logs will be my first step in forming a viable GNN-based hypothesis.


    /execute_action{review 378}'
