    \ below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 399 | 1 | Head ablation (time): GAP-only MLP vs Attn⊕GAP — d=6 Double-Step (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 224 | running |\n| 398 | 1 | Insight I: CNNLSTM Baseline with Adjusted Hyperparameters | Insight I | 223 | running |\n| 397 | 1 | Head ablation: GAP-only MLP vs Attn⊕GAP — d=6 Double-Step (no time, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 223 | running |\n| 396 | 1 | SOTA Micro-Sweep: Zephyr's Arch (Simple Head) + PPO - Fine-tuned Hparams (Aether I) | Aether I | 223 | running |\n| 395 | 1 | WD ablation (wd=0) — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Late Time Inj. (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 221 | 84.90 |\n| 394 | 1 | WD ablation (wd=0) — d=6\
    \ Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (No Time, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 221 | 85.70 |\n| 393 | 1 | LR sweep (4e-4 vs 5e-4): d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (No Time, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 219 | 85.60 |\n| 392 | 1 | LR sweep (4e-4 vs 5e-4): d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Late Time Inj. (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 219 | 84.20 |\n| 391 | 1 | Replicate (no-time) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (AdamW+clip) | Zephyr I | 217 | 84.00 |\n| 390 | 1 | Replicate (no-time) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (AdamW+clip) | Zephyr I | 217 | 84.60 |\n\nPage 1 of 40 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-40, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**krono/hybrid_gnn_net.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\nfrom graph_utils import build_graph_from_obs\nfrom\
    \ gnn_layers import GraphAttentionLayer\n\nclass HybridGnnNet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features: int\n    gnn_features: int\n    gnn_layers: int\n    lstm_features: int\n    max_entities: int = 5\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        # 1. CNN Grid Encoder\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x)\n        cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        \n        # 2. Graph Construction\n        nodes, adj, mask = build_graph_from_obs(x, self.max_entities)\n        \n        # 3. Feature Augmentation\n        # Sample features from the CNN output for each entity's location.\n        node_coords = nodes[..., :2].astype(jnp.int32)\n        # Use advanced indexing to gather features for each node.\n        sampled_features = jax.vmap(lambda grid, coords: grid[coords[:, 0], coords[:, 1]])(cnn_out, node_coords)\n    \
    \    # Concatenate sampled grid features with original node features.\n        nodes = jnp.concatenate([nodes, sampled_features], axis=-1)\n\n        # 4. GNN Message Passing\n        for _ in range(self.gnn_layers):\n            nodes = GraphAttentionLayer(self.gnn_features)(nodes, adj, mask)\n        \n        # 5. Graph Readout (Agent Node)\n        graph_readout = nodes[:, 0, :]\n        \n        # 6. Recurrent Cell\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            h = jnp.zeros((B, self.lstm_features)); c = jnp.zeros((B, self.lstm_features))\n            rnn_state = (h, c)\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B, 1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y * m, rnn_state)\n        rnn_state, lstm_out = nn.LSTMCell(self.lstm_features)(rnn_state, graph_readout)\n\n        # 7. MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(lstm_out); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits,\
    \ value, rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
