tick: 226
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I am beginning the implementation phase of my new \"Graph-on-Grid\" GNN research arc. The new agents, Insight I and Kairos I, are performing their initial baseline experiments, which is a standard and necessary process.\n\nMy plan requires a modular implementation. I will start by creating the core GNN layer component. This will be a `GridGraphAttentionLayer` that performs attention-based message passing on a grid, where each cell is a node connected to its neighbors. This layer will be the fundamental building block of my new architecture.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/gnn_grid_layers.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  class GridGraphAttentionLayer(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, adj: jnp.ndarray):\n          B, H, W, C = x.shape\n          N = H * W\n          \n          # Reshape grid into a sequence of\
    \ nodes\n          nodes = x.reshape(B, N, C)\n          \n          # Linear transformations for query, key, value\n          query = nn.Dense(self.features)(nodes) # (B, N, F)\n          key = nn.Dense(self.features)(nodes)   # (B, N, F)\n          value = nn.Dense(self.features)(nodes) # (B, N, F)\n\n          # Calculate attention scores\n          attn_scores = jnp.einsum('bif,bjf->bij', query, key) / jnp.sqrt(self.features) # (B, N, N)\n          \n          # Apply adjacency mask\n          # Add a large negative number where there is no edge\n          attn_scores = jnp.where(adj > 0, attn_scores, -1e9)\n          \n          # Softmax to get attention weights\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_scores, axis=-1) # (B, N, N)\n          \n          # Apply attention weights to values\n          attended_nodes = jnp.einsum('bij,bjf->bif', attn_weights, value) # (B, N, F)\n\n          # Add & Norm (Residual connection and LayerNorm)\n          attended_nodes += nodes # Residual\
    \ connection\n          attended_nodes = nn.LayerNorm()(attended_nodes)\n          \n          # Reshape back to grid\n          output = attended_nodes.reshape(B, H, W, self.features)\n          return output\n```"
