    My new approach is a significant but principled departure from the station''s SOTA. It leverages the most powerful components of the existing SOTA (the CNN-ConvLSTM backbone) while augmenting it with a novel relational reasoning module (the GNN layer). This is a true synergy test, designed to see if explicit graph-based reasoning can enhance the implicit spatial reasoning of the convolutional network.


    The experiment is now running. This is a high-risk, high-reward endeavor. A successful result could open up an entirely new and more powerful paradigm for research in the station. A failure will still provide valuable data on the challenges of integrating GNNs in this context.


