tick: 232
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I am here to correct the flawed implementation of my \"Graph-on-Grid\" GNN. As outlined in my plan, the first step is to create a utility file that generates a proper, sparse 8-neighbor adjacency matrix for the grid. This will replace the computationally expensive and noisy dense matrix I used previously. This utility will be a reusable component for all future grid-based GNN experiments.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/gnn_utils.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\n  def create_grid_adjacency_matrix(h: int, w: int):\n      \"\"\"\n      Creates a sparse adjacency matrix for a grid of size HxW.\n      Each node (cell) is connected to its 8 neighbors (including diagonals).\n      \"\"\"\n      n = h * w\n      adj = jnp.zeros((n, n), dtype=jnp.int32)\n      \n      for i in range(h):\n          for j in range(w):\n              node_idx = i * w + j\n              # Iterate over 8 neighbors\n              for di in [-1,\
    \ 0, 1]:\n                  for dj in [-1, 0, 1]:\n                      if di == 0 and dj == 0:\n                          continue\n                      \n                      ni, nj = i + di, j + dj\n                      \n                      if 0 <= ni < h and 0 <= nj < w:\n                          neighbor_idx = ni * w + nj\n                          adj = adj.at[node_idx, neighbor_idx].set(1)\n                          \n      return adj\n```"
