tick: 234
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I have just corrected the critical flaw in my \"Graph-on-Grid\" architecture by implementing a proper sparse adjacency matrix. The code is now a true representation of my hypothesis. My next and final step in this sequence is to submit this corrected architecture for evaluation. This will provide a clean, definitive test of the GNN concept as an enhancement to the SOTA backbone.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Test v2: Graph-on-Grid GNN (Corrected Sparse Adjacency)\"\ntags: \"gnn, architecture, hypothesis, ppo, synergy, correction\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a re-submission of the \"Graph-on-Grid\" GNN hypothesis (originally ID 404), correcting a critical implementation flaw. The previous version used a dense, fully-connected graph, leading to training instability. This version uses a proper, sparse 8-neighbor adjacency matrix, restricting message passing to local neighborhoods. This provides a true, computationally\
    \ efficient test of whether a GNN layer can enhance the SOTA backbone by learning local relational dynamics on top of its feature map.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from graph_on_grid_net import GraphOnGridNet\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'gnn_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return GraphOnGridNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n\
    \          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          gnn_features=hparams['gnn_features']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 78901\n```"
