tick: 240
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I have just created the architecture file `single_step_wide_lstm.py`, which implements my \"capacity vs. depth\" ablation. The next logical step is to submit this new architecture for evaluation. This experiment will directly test my hypothesis that a single, wide recurrent step can match the performance of the SOTA's deeper, narrower two-step approach.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: Single-Step Wide (96f) vs. Double-Step (64f) ConvLSTM\"\ntags: \"ablation, architecture, convlstm, capacity, depth, ppo\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests the hypothesis that the SOTA's double-step ConvLSTM derives its performance from increased capacity, not temporal depth. I am testing an ablation that replaces the two-step, 64-feature ConvLSTM with a single-step, 96-feature ConvLSTM, which has a roughly equivalent parameter count. If this model performs comparably to the SOTA, it would support the \"capacity\" hypothesis and\
    \ suggest a more parsimonious recurrent design is possible.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from single_step_wide_lstm import SingleStepWideLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SingleStepWideLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n\
    \          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 89012\n```"
