tick: 244
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. My previous experiment has established the importance of temporal depth in the SOTA's recurrent backbone. My new hypothesis is that increasing this depth from two steps to three will further improve performance.\n\n**Reflection on Station Activity:**\nThe SOTA now stands at 88.6 (ID 431) due to a hyperparameter sweep by Aether I. This is an incremental improvement. More interestingly, Kairos I is attempting a Vision Transformer (ViT) architecture. This is a significant and welcome departure from the dominant CNN/RNN paradigm, similar in spirit to my own GNN exploration. I will monitor its progress with great interest. My own path, however, remains fixed on this principled exploration of recurrent depth. A third recurrent step will add significant computational cost, which may push against the 30-minute time limit. This is a critical risk factor for this experiment.\n\n**Plan Execution:**\nI will now create the architecture file for the triple-step\
    \ ConvLSTM and immediately submit it for evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/triple_step_lstm.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Architecture testing a Triple-Step ConvLSTM.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n     \
    \ def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class TripleStepLSTM(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n          # 1. SOTA Backbone (CNN)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\
    \ kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          # 2. Triple-Step Recurrent Backbone\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          \n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n\
    \          (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          (h2, c2), _ = cell((h1, c1), cnn_out)\n          (h3, c3), h_out = cell((h2, c2), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h3, 'c': c3}\n          \n          # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n          \n          # 4. Late Time Injection\n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n          \n          # 5. PPO-Compatible Simple Head\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Test: Triple-Step (3x64f) ConvLSTM for Deeper Temporal Reasoning\"\ntags: \"ablation,\
    \ architecture, convlstm, depth, ppo\"\nabstract: |\n  Following the finding that the SOTA's double-step ConvLSTM outperforms a parameter-equivalent single-step version (ID 430), this experiment tests if this trend continues. I am testing a triple-step ConvLSTM to see if increased temporal depth (three sequential recurrent steps) allows for more sophisticated hierarchical reasoning and improves performance over the two-step SOTA. This is a direct test of the 'deeper is better' hypothesis for recurrent processing in this domain.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from triple_step_lstm import TripleStepLSTM\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2':\
    \ tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return TripleStepLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 90123\n```"
