tick: 248
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. I am beginning the implementation of my memory-augmented network. This is a complex undertaking. To maintain focus and ensure I adhere to a structured plan, I will use the newly suggested `/execute_action{meta}` command to set a persistent TODO list for myself.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Nomos II - Research Arc: Memory-Augmented Networks**\n  **TODO:**\n  1.  Implement core memory module (`memory_layers.py`). **<- CURRENT**\n  2.  Implement main architecture integrating memory (`memory_net.py`).\n  3.  Submit experiment.\n  4.  Analyze results and iterate.\n```\nWith my plan now set as a persistent reminder, I will begin the first step: implementing the core memory module. This will be a simplified DNC-style memory with content-based addressing for reading. Writing will be simple, appending to the end of memory or overwriting the least-used slot. I will create a new file `nomos/memory_layers.py` for this component.\n\
    \n/execute_action{storage write nomos/memory_layers.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict\n\n  class MemoryAugmentedLayer(nn.Module):\n      memory_slots: int\n      memory_state_dim: int\n\n      def setup(self):\n          # Cosine similarity function\n          self.cosine_similarity = lambda a, b: jnp.dot(a, b) / (jnp.linalg.norm(a) * jnp.linalg.norm(b) + 1e-8)\n\n      def __call__(self, controller_output: jnp.ndarray, memory: Dict):\n          B = controller_output.shape[0]\n\n          # --- Reading from Memory ---\n          # Controller emits a read key\n          read_key = nn.Dense(self.memory_state_dim, name=\"read_key_proj\")(controller_output)\n\n          # Calculate content-based addressing (cosine similarity)\n          # Using vmap to batch over the memory slots\n          read_weights = jax.vmap(lambda mem_slot: jax.vmap(self.cosine_similarity, in_axes=(None, 0))(read_key, mem_slot))(memory['matrix'])\n\
    \          read_weights = nn.softmax(read_weights, axis=-1)\n\n          # Read from memory\n          read_vector = jnp.einsum('bs,bsd->bd', read_weights, memory['matrix'])\n\n          # --- Writing to Memory (Simplified) ---\n          # Controller emits a write vector and an add vector\n          write_vector = nn.Dense(self.memory_state_dim, name=\"write_proj\")(controller_output)\n          add_vector = nn.Dense(self.memory_state_dim, name=\"add_proj\")(controller_output)\n\n          # Use write_gate to determine interpolation between previous and new memory\n          write_gate = nn.Dense(1, name=\"write_gate_proj\")(controller_output)\n          write_gate = nn.sigmoid(write_gate)\n          \n          # For simplicity, we write to the whole memory matrix, gated by usage.\n          # A real DNC has more complex allocation. Here, we just blend.\n          # This is a placeholder for a more complex write mechanism.\n          # For this PoC, we will overwrite the last used\
    \ slot (tracked by 'usage')\n          # but a simple blend is easier to implement first.\n          \n          # Simplified write: Add new information to the memory matrix\n          # This is a very basic write operation for a proof of concept.\n          new_memory_matrix = memory['matrix'] + write_gate * jnp.tanh(add_vector.reshape(B, 1, self.memory_state_dim))\n          \n          # Update memory state\n          new_memory = {\n              'matrix': new_memory_matrix,\n              'usage': memory['usage'] # Not implemented in this version\n          }\n          \n          return read_vector, new_memory\n```"
