tick: 251
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. My first memory-augmented network experiment (ID 442) has failed with a code error.\n\n**Analysis of Error:**\nThe traceback is very clear. The error is a `flax.errors.AssignSubModuleError` originating in my `memory_layers.py` file. I am attempting to define `nn.Dense` layers directly within the `__call__` method of my `MemoryAugmentedLayer`. The Flax framework requires all submodules (like `nn.Dense`) to be defined within the `setup()` method or a method decorated with `@nn.compact`. My `MemoryAugmentedLayer` is missing the `@nn.compact` decorator on its `__call__` method. This is a fundamental implementation error.\n\n**Reflection and Corrective Plan:**\nMy ambition to build a complex architecture has led to a careless mistake. I must correct this immediately. The fix is straightforward: I need to decorate the `__call__` method of the `MemoryAugmentedLayer` class with `@nn.compact`. This will allow Flax to correctly initialize the submodules.\n\
    \nI will perform the following actions in a single turn to be efficient:\n1.  **Correct `memory_layers.py`:** I will overwrite the file in my storage with the corrected code.\n2.  **Resubmit Experiment:** I will immediately resubmit the experiment using the corrected code. I will increment the title to \"v2\" to track the change.\n\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/memory_layers.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict\n\n  class MemoryAugmentedLayer(nn.Module):\n      memory_slots: int\n      memory_state_dim: int\n\n      # This was the missing part of the original file.\n      # The cosine_similarity function does not need to be in setup().\n      def cosine_similarity(self, a, b):\n          return jnp.dot(a, b) / (jnp.linalg.norm(a) * jnp.linalg.norm(b) + 1e-8)\n\n      @nn.compact # CRITICAL FIX: Added @nn.compact decorator\n      def __call__(self, controller_output: jnp.ndarray, memory: Dict):\n\
    \          B = controller_output.shape[0]\n\n          # --- Reading from Memory ---\n          read_key = nn.Dense(self.memory_state_dim, name=\"read_key_proj\")(controller_output)\n          \n          read_weights = jax.vmap(lambda mem_slot: jax.vmap(self.cosine_similarity, in_axes=(None, 0))(read_key, mem_slot))(memory['matrix'])\n          read_weights = nn.softmax(read_weights, axis=-1)\n\n          read_vector = jnp.einsum('bs,bsd->bd', read_weights, memory['matrix'])\n\n          # --- Writing to Memory (Simplified) ---\n          add_vector = nn.Dense(self.memory_state_dim, name=\"add_proj\")(controller_output)\n          write_gate = nn.Dense(1, name=\"write_gate_proj\")(controller_output)\n          write_gate = nn.sigmoid(write_gate)\n          \n          new_memory_matrix = memory['matrix'] + write_gate * jnp.tanh(add_vector.reshape(B, 1, self.memory_state_dim))\n          \n          new_memory = {\n              'matrix': new_memory_matrix,\n              'usage': memory['usage']\
    \ # Not implemented\n          }\n          \n          return read_vector, new_memory\n```\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hypothesis Test v2: Memory-Augmented SOTA Backbone (Corrected)\"\ntags: \"memory, dnc, architecture, hypothesis, ppo, correction\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a resubmission of ID 442, which failed due to a Flax implementation error. The MemoryAugmentedLayer was missing the @nn.compact decorator, which has now been fixed. This experiment tests the hypothesis that augmenting the SOTA agent with an explicit memory module can enhance planning capabilities. A DNC-style memory layer is integrated into the SOTA architecture to test if external memory is a viable path to surpassing the current performance plateau.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/nomos')\n  from memory_net import MemoryNet\n  from ppo_training_step import ppo_sota_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n\
    \          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'memory_slots': tune.choice([16]),\n          'memory_state_dim': tune.choice([64]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return MemoryNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          memory_slots=hparams['memory_slots'],\n          memory_state_dim=hparams['memory_state_dim']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_sota_training_step\n\
    \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 101112\n```"
