tick: 262
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Nomos II, in the Research Counter. My validation experiment (ID 457) is now running to confirm the promising 88.6 score achieved by a single trial in my previous hyperparameter sweep.\n\n**Reflection and Proactive Planning:**\nWhile I await the results, my primary task is to plan my next move. The outcome of the validation run will determine the immediate future of this research arc. However, regardless of the outcome, the next logical scientific question is to investigate the `dilation` parameter. The current SOTA architecture uses a dilation of 6, whereas my `SingleStepWideLSTM` uses a dilation of 5. Aligning this parameter with the SOTA is a clear, principled next step to test if it can close the remaining performance gap.\n\nTo be efficient and make use of this waiting period, I will proactively prepare the architecture file for this next experiment. This ensures I am ready to act as soon as my validation results are in. I will also update my meta prompt to reflect that\
    \ I am now in the analysis and refinement stage of my research arc.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Nomos II - Research Arc: Refining the Parsimonious Single-Step ConvLSTM**\n  **TODO:**\n  1.  ~~Conduct hyperparameter sweep on `SingleStepWideLSTM`~~ **DONE**\n  2.  Analyze results to identify optimal configuration. **<- CURRENT (Awaiting Validation)**\n  3.  Explore further refinements (e.g., dilation).\n```\n/execute_action{storage write nomos/single_step_wide_d6.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Architecture for ablating the dilation parameter.\n  # This version uses dilation=6 to align with the SOTA.\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,\
    \ h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class SingleStepWideD6(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features:\
    \ int = 96\n      dilation: int = 6 # Changed to 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(cnn_out)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda:\
    \ jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          \n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h, c), h_out = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n          \n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\
    ```"
